_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 5
---
order: 5
---
short_label: I.5
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In isosceles triangles the angles at the base equal one another, and, if the equal straight lines are produced further, then the angles under the base equal one another.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} be an isosceles triangle having the side {AB} equal to the side {AC}, and let the straight lines {BD} and {CE} be produced further in a straight line with {AB} and {AC}. [!just I.Def.20; I.Post.2]

I say that the angle {ABC|angBint} equals the angle {ACB}, and the angle {CBD} equals the angle {BCE}.

[!just I.3; I.Post.1]

Take an arbitrary point {F} on {BD}. Cut off {AG} from {AE} the greater equal to {AF} the less, and join the straight lines {FC} and {GB}.

